---
import { FULL_STOP, PERFECT, PERFECT_LENGTH, ROUGH, ROUGH_LENGTH } from '../handwriting';
---

<section id="why" class="px-3 sm:px-4" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="reveal rounded-card bg-surface px-6 py-20 text-center sm:px-12 sm:py-32">
    <p class="eyebrow text-ios-orange">Why it works</p>
    <h2 id="why-title" class="display mx-auto mt-6 max-w-5xl text-[clamp(2.6rem,6.6vw,5.75rem)]">
      Roughly right every day <span class="text-muted">beats perfectly right for a week.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-xl">
      You don't need to know that dinner was 612 calories. About 600 is close enough, and close enough every day
      tells you far more than a perfect week followed by nothing.
    </p>

    <!-- Two lines of handwriting: the loose one keeps going off the card, the neat one stops at a full stop.
         On a phone the drawing is wider than the card, so only the loose line's run-on is cropped. -->
    <figure class="why-lines reveal mx-auto mt-14 max-w-4xl overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] bg-white py-10 pl-5 sm:mt-20 sm:py-14 sm:pl-12">
      <svg
        class="block h-auto w-[150%] max-w-none sm:w-full"
        viewBox="96 670 1000 390"
        fill="none"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Two hand-drawn lines of loops, like joined-up handwriting. A loose green line, every loop a little different, keeps going past the edge. Below it, a neat grey line of seven identical loops stops with a full stop."
      >
        <path
          class="line line-rough"
          style={`--len:${ROUGH_LENGTH}px`}
          d={ROUGH}
          stroke="#34c759"
          stroke-width="12"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
        <path
          class="line line-perfect"
          style={`--len:${PERFECT_LENGTH}px`}
          d={PERFECT}
          stroke="#6e6e73"
          stroke-width="7"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
        <circle class="full-stop" cx={FULL_STOP.cx} cy={FULL_STOP.cy} r={FULL_STOP.r} fill="#6e6e73"></circle>
      </svg>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
